docker-library/wordpress/actions/runs/39627590069/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/docker-library/wordpress/actions/runs/39627590069/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/docker-library/wordpress/check-suites/107392188517","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/docker-library/wordpress/actions/runs/39627590069/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/docker-library/wordpress/actions/runs/39627590069/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/docker-library/wordpress/actions/runs/39627590069/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/docker-library/wordpress/actions/workflows/1146920","head_commit":{"id":"47909c264b81f4294696958fb70ed8fd3b299fef","tree_id":"948827821be1b16c02607e87e30e092d2666dd79","message":"Add mitigations for CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619\n\nOfficial PHP security advisory released on 21 Oct 2026 reports two critical\nunauthenticated Remote Code Execution vulnerabilities:\n\n1. CVE-2026-109618 (RCE via OOM corruption):\n   - Out-of-memory handling can interrupt PHP while internal request data\n     is only partially initialized.\n   - Mitigation: set 'memory_limit = -1' to avoid controllable PHP internal\n     OOM failure, with conservative 'post_max_size = 32M' and 'upload_max_filesize = 30M'.\n\n2. CVE-2026-109619 (RCE via stale global state):\n   - Request-owned internal state can survive after its backing memory has\n     been freed, allowing subsequent requests handled by the same worker\n     to reuse stale state.\n   - Mitigation: disable 'session.upload_progress.enabled = 0', and for PHP 8.5\n     set 'fatal_error_backtraces = 0'.\n\nRef: https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-21-5\nGHSA: GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w, GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:35:15Z","author":{"name":"Mr.Alidoosti","email":"mr.alidoosti@wallex.net"},"committer":{"name":"Mr.Alidoosti","email":"mr.alidoosti@wallex.net"}},"repository":{"id":20040409,"node_id"